From: Arvind Yadav <arvind.yadav@intel.com>
Subject: [PATCH] drm/xe: Resolve snapshot memory region under the bo reservation

xe_vm_snapshot_capture() reads bo->ttm.resource to record the memory
region of a mapped bo. That read is unlocked, and the resource is only
stable under the bo reservation, which xe_ttm_bo_purge() and the eviction
paths hold while freeing it. A purged bo therefore oopses on the NULL
resource, and adding a NULL test in place only narrows the window into a
use-after-free of the freed resource.

The reservation cannot be taken in xe_vm_snapshot_capture(): it runs in the
dma_fence_begin_signalling() section opened by devcoredump_snapshot(), and
vm->snap_mutex, held there, is itself taken under the reservation on the
gpuva insert and remove paths.

The region is only metadata, though, and nothing needs it before the dump
is formatted. Resolve it in xe_vm_snapshot_capture_delayed() instead, which
runs from a worker where the reservation can simply be taken. This is the
same pattern xe_lrc_snapshot_capture_delayed() already uses to read its bo.

That removes the unlocked resource dereference entirely rather than making
it less likely to crash. A bo found purged under the lock records -ENODATA,
which both consumers already handle, and skips the kvmalloc() of the VMA
length that would otherwise be freed again as soon as xe_bo_read() failed.

As a side effect the reported region and the captured data are now taken at
the same point. Previously the region came from hang time while the data
was read later in the worker, so an eviction in between made the two
disagree with no indication in the output.

Note this also changes the reported region for a mem_type outside the
switch, such as XE_PL_STOLEN, from 0 to unknown. Previously such a bo was
silently reported as system memory because uapi_mem_region kept its
kvzalloc() value.

Fixes: ad9843aac91a ("drm/xe/madvise: Implement purgeable buffer object support")
Signed-off-by: Arvind Yadav <arvind.yadav@intel.com>
---
diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/xe/xe_vm.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/xe/xe_vm.c
index 9e0176861c..fc8ad00e9c 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/xe/xe_vm.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/xe/xe_vm.c
@@ -4526,18 +4526,14 @@ struct xe_vm_snapshot *xe_vm_snapshot_capture(struct xe_vm *vm)
 			snap->snap[i].cpu_caching = bo->cpu_caching;
 			snap->snap[i].bo = xe_bo_get(bo);
 			snap->snap[i].bo_ofs = xe_vma_bo_offset(vma);
-			switch (bo->ttm.resource->mem_type) {
-			case XE_PL_SYSTEM:
-			case XE_PL_TT:
-				snap->snap[i].uapi_mem_region = 0;
-				break;
-			case XE_PL_VRAM0:
-				snap->snap[i].uapi_mem_region = 1;
-				break;
-			case XE_PL_VRAM1:
-				snap->snap[i].uapi_mem_region = 2;
-				break;
-			}
+			/*
+			 * The memory region is resolved in the delayed phase,
+			 * where the bo reservation can be taken. Reading
+			 * bo->ttm.resource here would be unlocked: this runs in
+			 * the dma-fence signalling path, and eviction or purge
+			 * can free the resource concurrently.
+			 */
+			snap->snap[i].uapi_mem_region = -1;
 		} else if (xe_vma_is_userptr(vma)) {
 			struct mm_struct *mm =
 				to_userptr_vma(vma)->userptr.notifier.mm;
@@ -4578,6 +4574,40 @@ void xe_vm_snapshot_capture_delayed(struct xe_vm_snapshot *snap)
 		    snap->snap[i].flags & XE_VM_SNAP_FLAG_IS_NULL)
 			continue;
 
+		if (bo) {
+			bool purged;
+
+			/*
+			 * bo->ttm.resource is only stable under the bo
+			 * reservation. Unlike xe_vm_snapshot_capture() this runs
+			 * from a worker, so the lock can be taken here; see
+			 * xe_lrc_snapshot_capture_delayed() for the same pattern.
+			 */
+			xe_bo_lock(bo, false);
+			purged = !bo->ttm.resource;
+			if (!purged) {
+				switch (bo->ttm.resource->mem_type) {
+				case XE_PL_SYSTEM:
+				case XE_PL_TT:
+					snap->snap[i].uapi_mem_region = 0;
+					break;
+				case XE_PL_VRAM0:
+					snap->snap[i].uapi_mem_region = 1;
+					break;
+				case XE_PL_VRAM1:
+					snap->snap[i].uapi_mem_region = 2;
+					break;
+				}
+			}
+			xe_bo_unlock(bo);
+
+			if (purged) {
+				/* Purged bo, nothing left to capture. */
+				snap->snap[i].data = ERR_PTR(-ENODATA);
+				goto cleanup_bo;
+			}
+		}
+
 		snap->snap[i].data = kvmalloc(snap->snap[i].len, GFP_USER);
 		if (!snap->snap[i].data) {
 			snap->snap[i].data = ERR_PTR(-ENOMEM);
